<exercisegroup cols="2" xml:id="exercisegroup-vectors-geometric-add" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
<title>Geometric addition of vectors</title>

<introduction><p>
	In each case,
	draw a vector addition triangle in the Cartesian plane that represents <m>\uvec{w} = \uvec{u} + \uvec{v}</m>,
	with the initial point of <m>\uvec{u}</m> at the origin.
	Then calculate the sum vector <m>\uvec{w}</m> and verify that its terminal point (from the origin) agrees with the terminal point of addition chain <m>\uvec{u} + \uvec{v}</m> on your diagram.
</p></introduction>

<exercise>

	<statement><p> <m> \uvec{u} = (-2,3) </m>, <m> \uvec{v} = (6,0) </m> </p></statement>

	<answer>

		<image width="61.1%">
			<latex-image label="image-vectors-exercises-geometric-add-answer-1">
				<xi:include href="geometric-add.d/answer-1.tex" parse="text" />
			</latex-image>
			<shortdescription> Diagram illustrating vector addition. </shortdescription>
			<description><p>
				A diagram consisting of a triangle in the <m>xy</m>-plane,
				with a directed line segment for each side.
				One side is a vector labelled <m>\uvec{u}</m>,
				extending from the origin to the point <m>P(-2,3)</m>.
				The next side is a vector labelled <m>\uvec{v}</m>,
				extending from <m>P</m> to the point <m>Q(4,3)</m>.
				The last side is a vector labelled <m>\uvec{w}</m>,
				extending from the origin to <m>Q</m>.
			</p></description>
		</image>

		<p><m> \uvec{w} = (-2,3) + (6,0) = (4,3) </m></p>

	</answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p> <m> \uvec{u} = (6,0) </m>, <m> \uvec{v} = (-2,3) </m> </p></statement>

	<answer>

		<image width="60%">
			<latex-image label="image-vectors-exercises-geometric-add-answer-2">
				<xi:include href="geometric-add.d/answer-2.tex" parse="text" />
			</latex-image>
			<shortdescription> Diagram illustrating vector addition. </shortdescription>
			<description><p>
				A diagram consisting of a triangle in the <m>xy</m>-plane,
				with a directed line segment for each side.
				One side is a vector labelled <m>\uvec{u}</m>,
				extending from the origin to the point <m>P(6,0)</m>.
				The next side is a vector labelled <m>\uvec{v}</m>,
				extending from <m>P</m> to the point <m>Q(4,3)</m>.
				The last side is a vector labelled <m>\uvec{w}</m>,
				extending from the origin to <m>Q</m>.
			</p></description>
		</image>

		<p><m> \uvec{w} = (6,0) + (-2,3) = (4,3) </m></p>

	</answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p> <m> \uvec{u} = (-2,-4) </m>, <m> \uvec{v} = (0,3) </m> </p></statement>

	<answer>

		<image width="43.2%">
			<latex-image label="image-vectors-exercises-geometric-add-answer-3">
				<xi:include href="geometric-add.d/answer-3.tex" parse="text" />
			</latex-image>
			<shortdescription> Diagram illustrating vector addition. </shortdescription>
			<description><p>
				A diagram consisting of a triangle in the <m>xy</m>-plane,
				with a directed line segment for each side.
				One side is a vector labelled <m>\uvec{u}</m>,
				extending from the origin to the point <m>P(-2,-4)</m>.
				The next side is a vector labelled <m>\uvec{v}</m>,
				extending from <m>P</m> to the point <m>Q(-2,-1)</m>.
				The last side is a vector labelled <m>\uvec{w}</m>,
				extending from the origin to <m>Q</m>.
			</p></description>
		</image>

		<p><m> \uvec{w} = (-2,-4) + (0,3) = (-2,-1) </m></p>

	</answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p> <m> \uvec{u} = (0,3) </m>, <m> \uvec{v} = (-2,-4) </m> </p></statement>

	<answer>

		<image width="34.7%">
			<latex-image label="image-vectors-exercises-geometric-add-answer-4">
				<xi:include href="geometric-add.d/answer-4.tex" parse="text" />
			</latex-image>
			<shortdescription> Diagram illustrating vector addition. </shortdescription>
			<description><p>
				A diagram consisting of a triangle in the <m>xy</m>-plane,
				with a directed line segment for each side.
				One side is a vector labelled <m>\uvec{u}</m>,
				extending from the origin to the point <m>P(0,3)</m>.
				The next side is a vector labelled <m>\uvec{v}</m>,
				extending from <m>P</m> to the point <m>Q(-2,-1)</m>.
				The last side is a vector labelled <m>\uvec{w}</m>,
				extending from the origin to <m>Q</m>.
			</p></description>
		</image>

		<p><m> \uvec{w} = (0,3) + (-2,-4) = (-2,-1) </m></p>

	</answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p> <m> \uvec{u} = (6,4) </m>, <m> \uvec{v} = (-2,-5) </m> </p></statement>

	<answer>

		<image width="59.4%">
			<latex-image label="image-vectors-exercises-geometric-add-answer-5">
				<xi:include href="geometric-add.d/answer-5.tex" parse="text" />
			</latex-image>
			<shortdescription> Diagram illustrating vector addition. </shortdescription>
			<description><p>
				A diagram consisting of a triangle in the <m>xy</m>-plane,
				with a directed line segment for each side.
				One side is a vector labelled <m>\uvec{u}</m>,
				extending from the origin to the point <m>P(6,4)</m>.
				The next side is a vector labelled <m>\uvec{v}</m>,
				extending from <m>P</m> to the point <m>Q(4,-1)</m>.
				The last side is a vector labelled <m>\uvec{w}</m>,
				extending from the origin to <m>Q</m>.
			</p></description>
		</image>

		<p><m> \uvec{w} = (6,4) + (-2,-5) = (4,-1) </m></p>

	</answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p> <m> \uvec{u} = (-2,-5) </m>, <m> \uvec{v} = (6,4) </m> </p></statement>

	<answer>

		<image width="70%">
			<latex-image label="image-vectors-exercises-geometric-add-answer-6">
				<xi:include href="geometric-add.d/answer-6.tex" parse="text" />
			</latex-image>
			<shortdescription> Diagram illustrating vector addition. </shortdescription>
			<description><p>
				A diagram consisting of a triangle in the <m>xy</m>-plane,
				with a directed line segment for each side.
				One side is a vector labelled <m>\uvec{u}</m>,
				extending from the origin to the point <m>P(-2,-5)</m>.
				The next side is a vector labelled <m>\uvec{v}</m>,
				extending from <m>P</m> to the point <m>Q(4,-1)</m>.
				The last side is a vector labelled <m>\uvec{w}</m>,
				extending from the origin to <m>Q</m>.
			</p></description>
		</image>

		<p><m> \uvec{w} = (-2,-5) + (6,4) = (4,-1) </m></p>

	</answer>

</exercise>

</exercisegroup>
